 "statement": "R3 cycle 3 (owner S75): what a phrase in a teaching sentence refers to, by general English role words (no category words). Checked in order; the phrase's head (subjectHead) is read first, then the whole phrase. A typed quantity (QK metric or kind) in the head is evidence of a measurement unless a claim cue is present. Used to check semantic type before any concept alignment: an identity needs a compatible concept kind. dn.1 development round 1 (development mentions only): achievement verbs and states as outcomes; generic hardware nouns and plural forms as product features.",
